  %% Algorithm: the reversible point-add construction
  Phases["Affine P plus Q in eight in-place phases: x -= Qx, y -= Qy, y /= x gives lambda, x += 3Qx, x -= lambda squared, y *= x, y -= Qy, x = Qx - x"]
  Coord["Coordinate blocks: classical-offset subtract, add 3Qx, final subtract and reverse subtract"]
  Square["Modular square: Karatsuba down to 64-bit schoolbook triangles; diagonal spread as ripple carry-in; measured top bits"]
  DivLeg["Division leg: seed rails from x, P1 = y/2, fused ticks to tick 136, late batch (rails alone, then payload with parked rails), endpoint, rails walk back"]
  MulLeg["Multiplication leg: rails-only forward walk, endpoint payload, mirrored late batch and fused reverse ticks, clear P1 = P0/2"]
  Walk["Leapfrog walk: two odd signed rails; per tick two forced add-halves, a deep or flat choice add-halve, then 0 to 3 extra halvings; 151 ticks, the last choice-only"]
  Tape["History tape: one 5-bit letter per tick; letters allocated only when each choice needs them"]
  Fused["Fused one-fold payload cell at room 60 or more: 17h = L + 17E - 16Nm mod 2^k; one 76-bit fold gives W* = W0 + jM - eps 2^k (F-1); E erased from a declared window; rotation by four"]
  Narrow["Narrow-room cells: one-place rotations instead of controlled shifts; a doubling form gives the multiply a room-24 cell; decreasing-bank folds"]
  Cleanup["Cleanup: rails parked at plus or minus 1 clear one payload against the other; reversing the walk consumes the tape and restores x; choice ancillas uncomputed by X measurement with phase repair; every phase returns scratch to zero"]

